ds better than the mark set by " [:a {:href "/athletes/94046"} "Kirsty Coventry"] " (ZIM) at the 2009 Worlds. Behind Franklin, Russian " [:a {:href "/athletes/115651"} "Anastasiya Zuyeva"] " closed fast for the silver medal in 2:05.92, while Franklin’s teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/112287"} "Elizabeth Beisel"] " won the bronze, as Simmonds dropped back to fourth. Coventry contested the final but was never a medal factor and finished sixth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Franklin became the sixth woman to win the 100/200 backstroke double, but the first since " [:a {:href "/athletes/93722"} "Diana Mocanu"] " (ROU) in 2000. This was her third gold medal of the 2012 Olympics, which she would finish with five medals and four golds."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126679"} "Missy Franklin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:07.54 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "2:06.84 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "2:04.06 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/115651"} "Anastasiya Zuyeva"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "2:09.36 (4 h3)"] [:td {} "2:07.88 (3 h1)"] [:td {} "2:05.92 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/112287"} "Elizabeth Beisel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.